1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,467
You stand on a bathroom scale.

2
00:00:02,467 --> 00:00:04,188
You sink into a mattress.

3
00:00:04,188 --> 00:00:06,559
A car stays parked on a steep road.

4
00:00:06,959 --> 00:00:09,357
Each time, a surface is pushing back.

5
00:00:09,357 --> 00:00:12,049
And that push is not
always what you think.

6
00:00:12,499 --> 00:00:15,590
Diya puts her pressure
cooker on the kitchen scale.

7
00:00:15,590 --> 00:00:17,201
It reads three kilograms.

8
00:00:17,551 --> 00:00:19,568
Then she presses down on the lid.

9
00:00:19,568 --> 00:00:21,724
The scale jumps to four and a half!

10
00:00:21,724 --> 00:00:23,827
But the cooker did not get heavier.

11
00:00:24,327 --> 00:00:26,765
So what is the scale really measuring?

12
00:00:26,765 --> 00:00:28,956
The answer is the normal reaction.

13
00:00:29,606 --> 00:00:31,702
So what is the normal reaction?

14
00:00:32,052 --> 00:00:35,609
When a body presses on a
surface, the surface pushes back.

15
00:00:35,609 --> 00:00:38,229
We call this push the normal reaction, N.

16
00:00:38,629 --> 00:00:40,259
Normal means perpendicular.

17
00:00:40,259 --> 00:00:44,453
N always points straight out of the
surface, at ninety degrees to it.

18
00:00:44,853 --> 00:00:46,410
It is a contact force.

19
00:00:46,410 --> 00:00:48,750
Lift the body off, and N is gone.

20
00:00:49,150 --> 00:00:51,075
And a surface can only push.

21
00:00:51,075 --> 00:00:52,405
It can never pull.

22
00:00:53,055 --> 00:00:54,604
To the motion notebook.

23
00:00:54,604 --> 00:00:56,945
A two kilogram box sits on a scale.

24
00:00:57,295 --> 00:01:00,787
Its weight, m g, is
nineteen point six newtons.

25
00:01:00,787 --> 00:01:04,498
The scale pushes up with
N, also nineteen point six.

26
00:01:04,898 --> 00:01:07,692
Now a hand presses down with ten newtons.

27
00:01:07,692 --> 00:01:09,703
The scale pushes back harder.

28
00:01:09,703 --> 00:01:12,085
N climbs to twenty nine point six.

29
00:01:12,485 --> 00:01:15,092
Now the hand lifts up with ten newtons.

30
00:01:15,092 --> 00:01:16,950
N drops to nine point six.

31
00:01:17,350 --> 00:01:20,880
On the graph, every newton
of push adds one newton to N.

32
00:01:20,880 --> 00:01:23,188
So a scale shows N, not your mass.

33
00:01:23,838 --> 00:01:26,704
Next, tilt the scale
into a ramp, and watch N.

34
00:01:27,054 --> 00:01:28,240
Slow-mo replay.

35
00:01:28,240 --> 00:01:30,168
Freeze at thirty degrees.

36
00:01:30,568 --> 00:01:32,307
Split the weight in two.

37
00:01:32,307 --> 00:01:34,971
m g cos theta presses into the surface.

38
00:01:34,971 --> 00:01:39,682
m g sine theta points down the slope,
and friction holds the box still.

39
00:01:40,082 --> 00:01:43,494
N only has to balance
the part that presses in.

40
00:01:43,494 --> 00:01:45,381
So N is m g cos theta.

41
00:01:45,381 --> 00:01:47,119
About seventeen newtons.

42
00:01:47,519 --> 00:01:48,481
Let it run.

43
00:01:48,481 --> 00:01:51,072
At sixty degrees, N is half of m g.

44
00:01:51,072 --> 00:01:53,594
The steeper the ramp, the smaller N.

45
00:01:54,244 --> 00:01:55,144
Your turn.

46
00:01:55,131 --> 00:01:59,014
You press a book flat against
a wall with fifteen newtons.

47
00:01:59,014 --> 00:02:00,217
It stays still.

48
00:02:00,217 --> 00:02:02,204
What is the normal reaction?

49
00:02:02,204 --> 00:02:03,509
Pause and decide.

50
00:02:06,709 --> 00:02:07,753
Fifteen newtons!

51
00:02:07,753 --> 00:02:10,090
The wall pushes back against your push.

52
00:02:10,090 --> 00:02:12,936
The weight points along
the wall, not into it.

53
00:02:13,586 --> 00:02:16,259
Now let's write it down,
one step at a time.

54
00:02:16,609 --> 00:02:17,509
Step one.

55
00:02:17,423 --> 00:02:21,015
The box does not sink in,
and it does not jump off.

56
00:02:21,015 --> 00:02:24,796
So the forces perpendicular
to the surface add up to zero.

57
00:02:25,546 --> 00:02:26,523
Step two.

58
00:02:26,523 --> 00:02:30,777
On a flat surface, N pushes
up and m g pulls down.

59
00:02:30,777 --> 00:02:32,695
N minus m g is zero.

60
00:02:32,695 --> 00:02:34,303
So N equals m g.

61
00:02:35,053 --> 00:02:36,113
Step three.

62
00:02:36,113 --> 00:02:38,257
Push down with a force F.

63
00:02:38,257 --> 00:02:40,896
Now N must hold up m g plus F.

64
00:02:40,896 --> 00:02:42,751
N equals m g plus F.

65
00:02:43,501 --> 00:02:44,448
Step four.

66
00:02:44,448 --> 00:02:46,298
Pull up with F instead.

67
00:02:46,298 --> 00:02:50,640
Your pull does part of the
job, so N equals m g minus F.

68
00:02:51,390 --> 00:02:52,403
Step five.

69
00:02:52,403 --> 00:02:56,979
On a ramp at angle theta,
only m g cos theta presses in.

70
00:02:56,979 --> 00:02:59,273
So N equals m g cos theta.

71
00:03:00,023 --> 00:03:01,102
Remember this.

72
00:03:01,102 --> 00:03:05,065
N is the surface pushing back,
and it is not always m g.

73
00:03:05,765 --> 00:03:06,823
Side by side.

74
00:03:06,823 --> 00:03:10,311
Push down on the box with
ten newtons, and N grows.

75
00:03:10,711 --> 00:03:13,225
Pull up with ten newtons, and N shrinks.

76
00:03:13,225 --> 00:03:15,499
Same box, same weight, different N.

77
00:03:16,099 --> 00:03:17,150
Now you try.

78
00:03:17,150 --> 00:03:20,772
Pull the two kilogram box
up with twenty five newtons.

79
00:03:20,772 --> 00:03:22,873
How hard does the scale push?

80
00:03:22,873 --> 00:03:24,179
Pause and decide.

81
00:03:27,379 --> 00:03:28,279
Zero!

82
00:03:27,952 --> 00:03:29,907
N can never go below zero.

83
00:03:29,907 --> 00:03:34,287
A surface can only push, so the
box simply lifts off the scale.

84
00:03:34,937 --> 00:03:36,672
Now, one worked example.

85
00:03:37,022 --> 00:03:39,065
Diya's cooker is three kilograms.

86
00:03:39,065 --> 00:03:41,943
She presses the lid down
with fifteen newtons.

87
00:03:41,943 --> 00:03:44,043
Find N, and the scale reading.

88
00:03:44,043 --> 00:03:45,611
g is nine point eight.

89
00:03:46,111 --> 00:03:48,623
The weight is three
times nine point eight.

90
00:03:48,623 --> 00:03:50,909
That is twenty nine point four newtons.

91
00:03:51,659 --> 00:03:54,868
She pushes down, so N equals m g plus F.

92
00:03:54,868 --> 00:03:57,489
Twenty nine point four plus fifteen.

93
00:03:57,489 --> 00:03:59,719
Forty four point four newtons.

94
00:04:00,469 --> 00:04:02,822
A scale shows N divided by g.

95
00:04:02,822 --> 00:04:07,916
Forty four point four over nine point
eight is about four point five three

96
00:04:07,916 --> 00:04:08,816
kilograms.

97
00:04:09,565 --> 00:04:11,463
That is the jump Diya saw.

98
00:04:11,463 --> 00:04:13,859
The cooker is still three kilograms.

99
00:04:13,859 --> 00:04:15,031
Only N changed.

100
00:04:15,681 --> 00:04:17,147
Now, the exam trap.

101
00:04:17,497 --> 00:04:21,504
On a ramp, many students
write N equals m g sine theta.

102
00:04:21,904 --> 00:04:25,251
Check it on flat ground,
where theta is zero.

103
00:04:25,251 --> 00:04:28,108
Sine zero is zero, so N would vanish.

104
00:04:28,108 --> 00:04:29,008
Wrong!

105
00:04:28,758 --> 00:04:31,465
Cos zero is one, so N equals m g.

106
00:04:31,465 --> 00:04:33,170
It must be cos theta.

107
00:04:33,820 --> 00:04:35,248
Where is this asked?

108
00:04:35,248 --> 00:04:39,579
In free-body numericals: blocks on
ramps, and blocks pushed or pulled at

109
00:04:39,579 --> 00:04:40,479
an angle.

110
00:04:40,965 --> 00:04:42,221
Exam level now.

111
00:04:42,221 --> 00:04:47,108
A two kilogram block sits on a smooth
ramp at thirty seven degrees, held

112
00:04:47,108 --> 00:04:49,130
still by a horizontal push.

113
00:04:49,130 --> 00:04:52,537
Sine thirty seven is
point six, and g is ten.

114
00:04:52,537 --> 00:04:54,389
Find the normal reaction.

115
00:04:54,389 --> 00:04:55,699
Pause and solve.

116
00:05:01,099 --> 00:05:02,462
The answer is C.

117
00:05:02,462 --> 00:05:03,972
Twenty five newtons.

118
00:05:04,472 --> 00:05:08,645
Along the slope, F cos theta
balances m g sine theta.

119
00:05:08,645 --> 00:05:10,640
So F is fifteen newtons.

120
00:05:11,140 --> 00:05:16,202
Into the surface, m g cos theta is
sixteen newtons, and F sine theta is

121
00:05:16,202 --> 00:05:17,102
nine.

122
00:05:17,306 --> 00:05:19,921
N balances both: twenty five newtons.

123
00:05:19,921 --> 00:05:22,097
So N can be bigger than m g!

124
00:05:22,697 --> 00:05:24,158
Here is your recap.

125
00:05:24,158 --> 00:05:25,660
Screenshot this card.

126
00:05:28,860 --> 00:05:30,790
Can you answer these without help?

127
00:05:31,190 --> 00:05:32,090
One.

128
00:05:31,645 --> 00:05:34,586
Why did the scale jump
when Diya pressed the lid?

129
00:05:35,486 --> 00:05:36,386
Two.

130
00:05:36,011 --> 00:05:38,769
Can a normal reaction ever pull a body?

131
00:05:39,669 --> 00:05:40,569
Three.

132
00:05:40,337 --> 00:05:45,685
On a ramp, why is N equal to m g
cos theta, and not m g sine theta?

133
00:05:46,585 --> 00:05:49,610
Next time: a rope lifts
a bucket out of a well.

134
00:05:49,610 --> 00:05:52,626
Is the pull in the rope
always the bucket's weight?

135
00:05:52,626 --> 00:05:54,157
We find out in tension.
